WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Hey, I've got some bad news!

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.110
I overheard something big.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.580
Apparently they're going to shelve
Daitokai.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.780
Shelve? Why?

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.180
I don't know!

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.220
I just overheard people talking about it
in the bathroom.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.090
Why?

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.790
Like I said, I don't know either.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.630
Anyway, let's get Araki-san and
Matsumoto-sensei here.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.360
That's a good idea.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.060
Okay, I'll call Araki-san then.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.800
I'll call Matsumoto-sensei.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.320
Great Passage

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:56.660
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:02.800
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:09.440
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:16.080
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:22.380
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:28.690
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.660
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:42.170
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:48.710
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:55.180
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.890
Steady Progress

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.700
The issue is most likely the budget.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.870
Daitokai

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.900
Dictionary making costs a lot of money
after all.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.240
So...

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.710
How about creating a summary of the
Genbu Japanese Learning Dictionary's

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.280
sales figures to use
as an earnings model?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.210
It's continuing to sell even now.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.180
Well...

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.290
I think the company already understands
that.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.390
This goes beyond just that.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.920
Perhaps it's important for us

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.530
to emphasize Daitokai's differences
from existing dictionaries.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.830
What do you think about submitting
the essay I wrote

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.800
when we first proposed Daitokai?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.500
We already submitted it
at the proposal meeting.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.910
Oh, I see.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.920
Why don't we start making outside
contracts for the manuscript?

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.950
What are you talking about?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.520
Hold on, just listen.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.190
I understand that it's early to be putting in
writing contracts.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:19.670
I haven't been working the last five years
in this department for nothing.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.470
Just get to the point!

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.670
In other words,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.710
we create an established entity.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.640
You know how close-knit this industry is.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.850
If we ask all the experts to help
with the dictionary,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.290
rumors of Daitokai will spread
like wildfire.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.990
I suppose it would.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:45.530
And if the company suddenly shelved
the project,

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.230
it wouldn't be good for their reputation.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.830
People will think their business
is in trouble.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.940
Or that they're only concerned
with immediate earnings.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.310
I see.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.580
Then the company won't be able to shelve
it so thoughtlessly.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.580
That is a very interesting idea!

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.810
-Good work, Nishioka!
-Right?

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.350
There goes his ego!

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.690
Can you blame me?

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.920
You get a free pass today!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.490
I was still in the middle of creating
the writing guidelines,

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.300
.but I will try to finish it
as soon as possible.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.400
Thank you!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.440
Then we will go forward with this and tell
them the guidelines will come later.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.670
I will do my best as well.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:38.680
So...

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.580
All right, that's the spirit, Majime!

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.920
We should narrow down which writers
we're interested in then.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.420
Sasaki-san.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.790
Please print out a list of candidates.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.990
Okay.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.910
Welcome home.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.340
Did I wake you?

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.980
After that frantic call you gave me earlier--

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.010
I will be late today, but please don't worry
about me!

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:18.650
--how am I supposed to go to sleep?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:19.890
I'm sorry.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.020
So, what happened?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.390
Well, actually--

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm home.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.860
Oh, welcome home.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.070
You're still up?

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.070
Well, it seems something happened
with Micchan.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.340
Micchan. Something happened
to Majime-san?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:42.740
Oh, just call him Micchan already! Right?

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.980
Yes.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.790
So that's why you were acting like that.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.660
-Yes.
-I can't imagine.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.490
Then you and your team
aren't going to give up, are you?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:00.660
No.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.700
Are you okay?

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.870
I'm okay! Yes.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.500
Come on, Micchan. Eat your ramen
and try to relax.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.140
Yeah, or they'll get soggy.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.910
Okay. Thank you for the meal.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.550
Micchan really loves this dish.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.780
Oh, love? Yes.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.520
But it's good.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:28.920
Really? Let me see.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.730
I think this turned out better than usual.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.560
You eat it a lot too?

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.000
Micchan shares it with me
from time to time.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:12.700
A writing guideline outlines the process
for the entries that include

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.700
information, number of letters,
formatting,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.870
and also includes
concrete examples.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.440
Writing Guideline
2nd Draft

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:23.040
Majime, why don't you take a break
from collecting entries

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:27.910
and work on this writing guideline
with Matsumoto-sensei?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.050
Okay.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.480
Once the writing guideline is complete,

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.450
the editorial department will write
the example manuscript.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.160
After actually doing the work,

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:42.930
we'll check to see if there are any holes
or shortcomings in the writing guideline.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.900
Normally we'd hand these two things
to the contract writers,

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.170
but as we discussed yesterday,
we will be handing them out later.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.610
Leave that to me.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.780
I will be sure to express to the writers

00:07:55.940 --> 00:08:00.010
just how much we'd appreciate
their help.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.850
All right then,

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.120
Sasaki-san, could you make
the appointments?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.250
Of course.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:09.190
I'm going to make so many calls too.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.230
I'll head over to the main building
and gather some intel.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:16.560
All right, well, good luck
to each of you then.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.900
Good morning.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.730
Good morning.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.170
Yes, our dictionary will be called Daitokai.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.140
Yes, that's right.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.140
We would love to collaborate with you.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.040
It's me! Nishioka from Genbu.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.750
Regarding kanji notation,

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:39.150
my thought is to have the writers write
freely at first.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.890
What if they use an uncommon
kanji character?

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:50.300
If that happens, we will aggressively add
notation to make it easier to understand.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.130
I see.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.170
All right! I got an appointment
with Mori-sensei.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.200
We're counting on you, Nishioka.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.070
-Good luck!
-Yeah!

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:04.180
I'll go put it in the bag!

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.210
Dictionary editorial department

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.030
You're still doing that?
You were working on that last month.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.160
Genbu Books Publishing

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.230
Yes. It looks like it'll take a little longer.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:38.670
Well, I guess it would take this long.

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:43.010
There's no end
when it comes to making dictionaries.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.310
Nishioka-san!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:49.850
Hello there.

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.750
I heard about your company's...

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:54.890
Daitokai.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.420
That's right. That. I hear it's coming along.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:02.660
But it seems like you've been
pretty proactive yourself.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.970
Are you in trouble or something?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.070
Yeah! Come on.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.740
Everything's going great!

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:13.970
See you later!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.810
Bye.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:20.450
Is Nishioka-san really okay?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.820
I bet Genbu's upper management
is pissed.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.990
Of course he's not okay, stupid.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.720
They won't let him off easy
for what he's done.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.220
Man, I'd be scared.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.190
That's how it goes.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.060
The nail that sticks out gets hammered in.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.900
Hello, everyone!

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.130
Everything's coming along nicely!

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:42.400
What is?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:46.810
I'm talking about everything we've been
doing these last few months.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:50.040
The rumors are spreading like we hoped.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.180
Really?

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:55.210
Yes, I just heard someone outside
mention it.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:56.950
Actually said the word Daitokai.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.350
Really?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.050
Everyone's hard work has paid off.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:05.720
Daitokai has taken another step further.

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.230
Yes.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.130
Thank goodness.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.230
All right, we've come this far.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:15.030
All that's left is to wait
for how the company reacts.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.950
I've made up my mind.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.480
I'm taking this weekend off.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.290
Hey, Majime.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.420
You take it off too.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.860
Listen to me.

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.160
Sometimes you need to forget about work.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.830
You can't come up with good ideas
unless you give your mind a break.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.030
He is right.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.770
There are certain experiences that are
only available on the weekend,

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:52.270
like voices, smells,
and expressions too.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:57.940
They may lead to opportunities
to discover new words.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.810
So it just comes back to words?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.350
Yes, of course.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.420
Well, I'm going home then.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.990
Good night.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.890
Oh, before I forget. Majime.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.090
Since you're taking the weekend off,
you've gotta ask Kaguya out on a date.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.430
Give your mind a break.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.570
You might make new discoveries.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.200
Bye, then.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:36.150
I have to admit, Nishioka's idea caught me
by surprise.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:38.450
He's quite something.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.160
Yes. That ability to take action
is very like him.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.930
We're starting to become a good team.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.860
Yes.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.530
Wow, look how easy it is to cook
with them.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.000
Man.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:58.400
Getting invited out by one of the writers
we've contracted.

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:03.340
He just kept talking about mammal
hibernation the whole time.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:08.050
Hey, you haven't been complaining
about work at all lately.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.920
I haven't?

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:15.420
In any case, dictionary making
sure isn't normal.

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:18.290
There's no end to the work
and time involved,

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.430
and it's real mundane.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:23.630
It's work for masochists.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.430
Majime is definitely a masochist.

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:30.470
Oh, that weird guy?

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:33.570
Yeah. That guy is totally weird.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:36.880
He's a real freak
when it comes to dictionary making.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.010
Freak?

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:41.080
He just gets lost in his work
like you wouldn't believe.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:43.550
You talk to him and he doesn't hear you
at all.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:47.290
He just mutters at his desk
and never eats.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:52.090
It might just be the perfect job for him.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.260
I mean, what other job could he even do?

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.960
Did you know he's a virgin?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.100
I don't think being a virgin matters.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:07.070
To be honest, I don't have that same
passion for words.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.510
He's real amazing.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.450
But you know,

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:19.420
I have something he doesn't.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:23.390
I'll play to my strengths
and get things done.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.290
I mean, I had to listen to a professor drone
on about bears for three and a half hours.

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:31.400
All while downing booze.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:36.500
Looks like I'll be hibernating tomorrow.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:41.240
I might be bald by the time we finish.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.040
I'm definitely going to be bald.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.180
What's wrong with being bald?
Saint Francis was bald.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:50.950
Why Saint Francis?

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.720
I think I'll have another.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.190
Now, I'm sure you're all wondering
the price!

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.420
Including everything we're offering,

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.230
here it is.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.700
It's just 19,800 yen!

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:45.310
Micchan.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.450
Are you off today?

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.080
Yes.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.590
I see. How has work been?

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:56.390
It's started to settle down just a little.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.690
So, in that vein,

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.260
apparently it's very important
to give my mind a break.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.830
According to Nishioka-san.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.470
So...

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.770
Do you have the day off as well?

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:13.110
Yes.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.410
I see.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:22.680
What a beautiful day!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.620
Why don't you two go out somewhere?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.360
Let's do that.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.310
Take-san,

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:47.410
is she having vision problems?

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.140
Is she?

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:55.320
She scrunched her face like this
several times earlier.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.820
I'm worried.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.620
Oh, that.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:01.320
I think she was trying to wink at you.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:04.490
Wink?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:12.430
It seems like Grandma set us up.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.850
Do you think that's moving up there?

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:28.580
It was moving.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:29.850
Yes.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:33.320
It never looks like it's moving
when you see it from the Souunsou.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.600
It's been moving all this time.

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:51.840
Ferris wheels are similar to cooking.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:55.640
No matter how delicious the meal
you make is,

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.480
it's not the end,

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.250
but actually the beginning.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.450
That's...

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.350
There's no such thing
as the perfect meal.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.930
Or an idea of actually being finished.

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:15.230
But you still...

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.930
Yes, I still want to do it.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:19.770
I want to keep cooking.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:23.410
I feel the same!

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.910
Dictionaries,

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.540
and making dictionaries.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.590
Yes.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:43.490
I...

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.800
Of all the rides in an amusement park,

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.370
the Ferris wheel

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.370
is my favorite.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.280
Me too.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.570
Steady Progress

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:29.370
To move forward step by step
I will move forward despite difficulty

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:44.420
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:55.430
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:07.080
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:13.980
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:19.820
So please stay the way you are

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:25.930
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:31.400
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:44.110
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.060
Micchan--

00:21:57.660 --> 00:21:59.760
The Ferris wheel continues to turn

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:02.930
with me still inside
after I missed my chance to get off.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:04.570
Micchan.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.640
I hope he'll be able to get off next time.
